# ------------------------------------------------------------------ data
# `data/` and `output/` are symlinks into ../ov-vidvrd-lab on the dev machine
# (42 GB of VidVRD frames, ~9 GB of checkpoints). Neither belongs in git, and a
# symlink pointing outside the repo is meaningless in a clone.
# Set them up per docs/22_Data-pipeline.md, then check with `python -m utils.paths`.
data/
output/

# model weights, feature banks and extracted frames, wherever they land
*.pth
*.pth.tar
*.pt
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
*.pkl
*.npy
*.npz
*.h5

# ------------------------------------------------------------- the paper
# The METOR paper is on arXiv (2505.06663) and does not need redistributing
# here. NOTE: docs/figures/*.png are cropped from it and ARE tracked -- arXiv
# publishes it under CC-BY 4.0, which permits that with attribution.
*.pdf

# --------------------------------------------------------- CUDA extension
# Built by ops/make.sh; must be compiled per machine, never committed.
ops/build/
ops/*.egg-info/
ops/**/*.so

